\pard\sb320\sa60\cf1\b\fs52 01\cf2\fs36   What is a Watchdog?\cf0\b0\fs22\par

\pard\sa200\cf3\fs20 The core concept behind ANKITA's always-on intelligence layer\cf0\fs22\par

\pard\sb160\sa160\par

\pard\sb120\sa120\cf5 Right now ANKITA reacts. \i You ask \f4\u8594?\f1  \f2 she answers. Jarvis doesn't work like that. \i0 Jarvis runs in the background 24/7, watching prices, scanning news, monitoring your files and git repos \f4\emdash\f1  \b\f2 and alerts you the moment something matters. \b0 That's a Watchdog.\cf0\par

\pard\sb80\sa80\cf5\lang9 A Watchdog is a \cf1\b persistent background daemon thread\cf5\b0  that continuously monitors ONE thing \f1\emdash  \f2 at a configurable interval \f1\emdash  \f2 and fires an alert (via ProactiveEngine) when a condition is met. Each Watchdog:\cf0\par

\pard\fi-360\li720\sb80\sa80\cf1\f1\bullet\cf5    \f2 Runs in its own daemon thread inside HiveMind \f1\emdash  \f2 never blocks ANKITA\cf0\par
\cf1\f1\bullet\cf5    \f2 Has configurable poll interval, threshold, and alert cooldown\cf0\par
\cf1\f1\bullet\cf5    \f2 Self-heals: auto-restarts on crash with exponential backoff\cf0\par
\cf1\f1\bullet\cf5    \f2 Persists its state to disk \f1\emdash  \f2 survives ANKITA restarts\cf0\par
\cf1\f1\bullet\cf5    \f2 Integrates with ProactiveEngine to push alerts to the GUI/chat\cf0\par

\pard\sb160\par
